===Etymology 1===
{{root|en|ine-pro|*kh₂eyd-}}
From {{inh|en|enm|hitten||to hit, strike, make contact with}}, from {{inh|en|ang|hittan||to meet with, come upon, fall in with}}, from {{der|en|non|hitta||to strike, meet}}, from {{der|en|gem-pro|*hittijaną|t=to come upon, find}}, from {{der|en|ine-pro|*kh₂eyd-|t=to fall; fall upon; hit; cut; hew}}.

Cognate with {{cog|is|hitta||to meet}}, {{cog|da|hitte||to find}}, {{cog|la|caedō||to kill}}, {{cog|sq|qit||to hit, throw, pull out, release}}.

====Verb====
{{en-verb|||hit|past2=hat|past2_qual=dialectal, obsolete|past3=het|past3_qual=rare, dialectal|past_ptc2=hitten|past_ptc2_qual=archaic, rare, dialectal}}
[[File:Boxing at 2016 summer Olympic Games in Rio-de-Janeiro.jpg|thumb|Two boxers '''hitting''' each other]]

# {{lb|en|heading|physical}} ''To [[strike]].''
## {{lb|en|transitive}} To administer a [[blow]] to, directly or with a weapon or missile.
##: {{ux|en|One boy '''hit''' the other.}}
##* {{RQ:Jefferies Amateur Poacher|chapter=II|passage=Orion '''hit''' a rabbit once; but though sore wounded it got to the bury, and, struggling in, the arrow caught the side of the hole and was drawn out. Indeed, a nail filed sharp is not of much avail as an arrowhead; you must have it barbed, and that was a little beyond our skill.}}
##* {{quote-book|en|year=1922-1927|author=w:Frank Harris|title=w:My Life and Loves|passage=He tried to '''hit''' me but I dodged the blow and went out to plot revenge.}}
##* {{RQ:Joyce Ulysses|chapter=[Episode 15]|passage={{smallcaps|Bello}}: (Shouts) Good, by the rumping jumping general! That's the best bit of news I heard these six weeks. Here, don't keep me waiting, damn you! (He slaps her face)<br />{{smallcaps|Bello}}: (Whimpers) You're after '''hitting''' me. I'll tell{{nb...}}}}
##* {{quote-book|en|year=1934|author=w:Robert E. Howard|title=The Slugger's Game|passage=I hunted him for half a hour, aiming to learn him to '''hit''' a man with a table-leg and then run, but I didn't find him.}}
## {{lb|en|transitive}} To come into [[contact]] with forcefully and suddenly.
##: {{ux|en|The ball '''hit''' the fence.}}
##* {{RQ:Swift Gulliver's Travels|II|passage=a dozen apples, each of them near as large as a Bristol barrel, came tumbling about my ears; one of them '''hit''' me on the back as I chanced to stoop, and knocked me down flat on my face.}}
##* {{quote-book|en|year=1882|author=w:Nathaniel Hawthorne|title=Doctor Grimshawe's Secret: A romance|passage=Meanwhile the street boys kept up a shower of mud balls, many of which '''hit''' the Doctor, while the rest were distributed upon his assailants.}}
## {{lb|en|intransitive}} To strike against something.
##* {{RQ:Locke Malebranche|passage=If bodies be extension alone, {{...}}how can they move and '''hit''' one against another?}}
## {{lb|en|transitive}} To activate a [[button]] or [[key]] by [[press]]ing and releasing it.
##: {{ux|en|'''Hit''' the Enter key to continue.}}
## {{lb|en|transitive|slang}} To kill a person, usually on the instructions of a third party.
##: {{ux|en|'''Hit''' him tonight and throw the body in the river.}}
##* '''1973''', Mario Puzo, Francis Ford Coppola, ''The Godfather Part II'' (screenplay, second draft)
##*: FREDO: Mikey, why would they ever '''hit''' poor old Frankie Five-Angels? I loved that ole sonuvabitch.
## {{lb|en|transitive|military}} To attack, especially amphibiously.
##: {{ux|en|If intelligence had been what it should have been, I don't think we'd ever have '''hit''' that island.}}
## {{label|en|figurative|ambitransitive}} To affect someone, as if dealing a blow to that person.
##: {{ux|en|Their coffee really '''hits''' the spot.}}
##: {{ux|en|I used to listen to that song all the time, but it '''hits''' different(ly) now.}}
# {{label|en|transitive}} To manage to [[touch]] (a target) in the right place.
#: {{antonyms|en|miss}}
#: {{ux|en|I '''hit''' the jackpot.}}
# {{lb|en|transitive|colloquial}} To [[switch on]].
#: {{antonyms|en|cut|kill}}
#: {{ux|en|Somebody's been here! '''Hit''' the lights!}}
# {{lb|en|transitive|music|informal}} To [[commence]] playing.
#: {{ux|en|I'd love to hear your band play. <br>'''Hit''' it boys!}}
# {{lb|en|transitive|colloquial}} To briefly visit.
#: {{ux|en|We '''hit''' the grocery store on the way to the park.}}
# {{lb|en|transitive|informal}} To [[encounter]] an [[obstacle]] or other [[difficulty]].
#: {{ux|en|You'll '''hit''' some nasty thunderstorms if you descend too late.}}
#: {{ux|en|We '''hit''' a lot of traffic coming back from the movies.}}
# {{lb|en|heading}} ''To attain, to achieve.''
## {{lb|en|transitive|informal}} To [[reach]] or [[achieve]].
##: {{ux|en|The movie '''hits''' theaters in December.}}
##: {{usex|en|The temperature could '''hit''' 110°F tomorrow.}}
##: {{usex|en|We '''hit''' Detroit at one in the morning but kept driving through the night.}}
##* {{quote-video game|en|year=2004|title=w:Paper Mario: The Thousand-Year Door|developer=Intelligent Systems|publisher=Nintendo|system=GameCube|level=Rogueport|translator=Nintendo of America|text=As soon as we '''hit''' Jazzafrazz Town, we were overcome by the glitz and the glamour.}}
##* {{quote-journal|en|year=2012 August 1|author=Owen Gibson|title=London 2012: rowers Glover and Stanning win Team GB's first gold medal|journal=Guardian Unlimited|url=http://www.guardian.co.uk/sport/2012/aug/01/london-2012-glover-stanning-gb-gold|passage=And her success with Glover, a product of the National Lottery-funded Sporting Giants talent identification programme, will also spark relief among British officials who were starting to fret a little about '''hitting''' their target of equalling fourth in the medal table from Beijing.}}
## {{lb|en|intransitive}} To meet or reach what was aimed at or desired; to succeed, often by luck.
##* {{RQ:Shakespeare All's Well|act=II|scene=i|passage=And oft it '''hits''' / Where hope is coldest and despair most fits.}}
##* {{RQ:Swift On Poetry|page=3|lines=1–2|passage=All Human Race wou’d fain be ''Wits'', / And Millions miſs, for one that '''hits'''.}}
## To [[guess]]; to [[light upon]] or [[discover]].
##* {{RQ:Shakespeare Taming of the Shrew|act=II|scene=i|passage=Thou hast '''hit''' it.}}
##* {{RQ:Tennyson In Memoriam|XLVI|69|And we shall sit at endless feast,<br>⁠Enjoying each the other’s good;<br>⁠What vaster dream can '''hit''' the mood<br>Of Love on earth?}}
# {{lb|en|transitive}} To [[affect]] [[negatively]].
#: {{ux|en|The economy was '''hit''' by a recession.&emsp; {{nowrap|The hurricane '''hit''' his fishing business hard.}}}}
# {{lb|en|metaphorically}} To [[attack]].
#* {{quote-web|en|date=2016-03-03|author=Nick Gass|quotee=Donald Trump|work=Politico|title=Trump on small hands: 'I guarantee you there's no problem'|url=https://www.politico.com/blogs/2016-gop-primary-live-updates-and-results/2016/03/donald-trump-small-hands-220223|text=I have to say this, he '''hit''' my hands. Nobody has ever '''hit''' my hands. I’ve never heard of this one. Look at those hands. Are they small hands?}}
# {{lb|en|heading|games}} ''To make a play.''
## {{lb|en|transitive|cards}} In [[blackjack]], to deal a card to.
##: {{ux|en|'''Hit''' me.}}
## {{lb|en|intransitive|baseball}} To come up to bat.
##: {{ux|en|Jones '''hit''' for the pitcher.}}
## {{lb|en|backgammon}} To take up, or replace by a [[piece]] belonging to the opposing player; said of a single [[unprotected]] piece on a [[point]].
# {{lb|en|transitive|computing|programming}} To [[use]]; to [[connect]] to.
#: {{ux|en|The external web servers '''hit''' DBSRV7, but the internal web server '''hits''' DBSRV3.}}
# {{lb|en|transitive|US|slang}} To have [[sex]] with.
#: {{ux|en|I'd '''hit''' that!}}
# {{lb|en|transitive|US|slang}} To inhale an amount of smoke from a narcotic substance, particularly [[marijuana]].
#* {{quote-song|en|lyricist=Jordan Houston; Darnell Carlton; Paul Beauregard; Premro Smith; Marlon Goodwin; David Brown; Willie Hutchinson|passage=Tastes like fruit when you '''hit''' it; got to have bread to get it.|url=https://genius.com/Three-6-mafia-stay-fly-lyrics|title=Stay Fly|publisher=Sony BMG|year=2005|album=Most Known Unknown|artist=Three 6 Mafia (featuring Young Buck, 8 Ball, and MJG)}}
# {{lb|en|transitive|bodybuilding}} (of an exercise) to [[affect]], to [[work]] a [[body part]].
#: {{ux|en|This is another great exercise which '''hits''' the long head.}}
# {{lb|en|transitive|bodybuilding}} To [[work out]].
#: {{ux|en|With that said, the group '''hitting''' their legs just once a week still made gains.}}

