====Noun====
{{en-noun}}

# A [[blow]]; a [[punch]]; a striking against; the collision of one body against another; the stroke that touches anything.
#* {{RQ:Dryden Juvenal Satires|4|passage=So he the fam'd Cilician fencer prais'd, / And, at each '''hit''', with wonder seem'd amaz'd.}}
#: {{ux|en|''The '''hit''' was very slight.''}}
# {{senseid|en|success}} Something very successful, such as a [[song]], [[film]], or [[video game]], that receives widespread recognition and [[acclaim]].
#* {{quote-journal|en|year=1848|journal=The Musical World|volume=23|title=Her Majesty's Theatre
|url=https://books.google.ca/books?id=_PksAAAAYAAJ&pg=PA114&dq=%22be+a+hit%22
|text=Marie Taglioni was another '''hit''' for Her Majesty's Theatre last season, and will be a '''hit''' again this season{{...}}}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|date=February 9, 2012| author=Tasha Robinson| title=Film: Review: Chico & Rita| url=http://www.avclub.com/articles/chico-rita,69067/| passage=''Chico & Rita'' opens in the modern era, as an aged, weary Chico shines shoes in his native Cuba. Then a song heard on the radio—a '''hit''' he wrote and recorded with Rita in their youth—carries him back to 1948 Havana, where they first met.}}
# {{lb|en|figuratively}} A blow; a calamitous or damaging occurrence.
#: {{ux|en|His reputation took a '''hit''' when the new information came to light.}}
# An attack on a location, person or people.
# A [[collision]] of a [[projectile]] with the [[target]].
#* {{quote-journal|en|date=2022 January 12|author=Benedict le Vay|title=The heroes of Soham...|journal=RAIL|issue=948|page=43|text=But signalman Bridges was never to answer driver Gimbert's desperate question. A deafening, massive blast blew the wagon to shreds, the 44 high-explosive bombs exploding like simultaneous '''hits''' from the aircraft they should have been dropped from. The station was instantly reduced to bits of debris, and the line to a huge crater.}}
## In the game of ''[[w:Battleship (game)|Battleship]]'', a correct guess at where one's opponent ship is.
# {{lb|en|computing|Internet}} A [[match]] found by searching a computer system or [[search engine]]
# {{lb|en|Internet}} A measured visit to a [[web site]], a request for a single file from a web server.
#: {{ux|en|My site received twice as many '''hits''' after being listed in a [[search engine]].}}
# An approximately correct answer in a [[test set]].
# {{lb|en|baseball}} The complete play, when the [[batter]] reaches [[base]] without the benefit of a [[walk]], [[error]], or fielder’s choice.
#: {{ux|en|The catcher got a '''hit''' to lead off the fifth.}}
# {{lb|en|colloquial}} A dose of an illegal or addictive drug.
#: {{ux|en|Where am I going to get my next '''hit'''?}}
# A premeditated [[murder]] done for criminal or political purposes.
#* {{quote-journal|en|author=Megan K. Stack|title=He Was Shot 14 Times at the Dinner Table. His Children Want to Know if Britain Ordered the Hit.|work=The New York Times|date=2023-08-30|url=https://www.nytimes.com/2023/08/30/opinion/finucane-assassination-northern-ireland.html|issn=0362-4331|author2=Rob Stothard|passage=The questions that have always haunted the family — who ordered the '''hit''', and why, and who in London might have known — remain unanswered.}}
# {{lb|en|dated}} A peculiarly apt expression or turn of thought; a phrase which hits the mark.
#: {{ux|en|a happy '''hit'''}}
#* {{RQ:Pope Essay on Man|passage=What late he called a blessing, now was wit, / And God's good providence, a lucky '''hit'''.}}
# {{lb|en|backgammon}} A move that throws one of the opponent's men back to the entering point.
# {{lb|en|backgammon}} A game won after the adversary has removed some of his men. It counts for less than a [[gammon]].

