==Swedish==

===Etymology 1===
From {{der|sv|gmq-osw|-}} ''hit'', from *''hī''+''at''.
* ''hī'', from {{der|sv|ine-pro|*kei-}} (as in {{cog|grc|ἐκεῖ}})
* ''at'', from {{der|sv|gem-pro|*at}}, from {{der|sv|ine-pro|*ád}} (as in Swedish {{m|sv|åt}})
Composed in a similar way: {{cog|is|hegat}} and {{m|is|hingað}}.
